tween T2 and W2, maybe T2 is safer. The user has already played T2, so others might have it. Also, T2 is part of T1-T2-T3, which they don't have T3. So discarding T2 is probably the safest move here.\n</think>\n\nEvaluation: [The hand contains a mix of terminals, mid-numbered suits, and honors. The key is to discard a tile that doesn't hinder potential patterns like Chicken Hand (8 points) or All Simples (2 points). T2 is part of a partial chow (T1-T2-T3) but lacks completion, making it a safe discard.]\nReason: [T2 is a mid-numbered tile with no supporting tiles for a chow (T1 is present, but T3 is not). Discarding it preserves concealed hand potential and avoids giving others a complete meld. Other terminals (T1, T9) and honors (F2, F3, J3) are safer but may be more valuable for scoring patterns.]\nAnswer: Play T2"}
